{# The worker profile, run by every sub-agent the lead delegates to.

   **No plan-first block, and not by omission.** `_blocks/plan_first.md.j2` renders only
   where the todo writers are bound, and a worker binds none of them
   (`subagents.WORKER_DENIED_TOOLS`), so the block is empty here whatever this template
   does. A worker has one objective and a few tool turns; a plan is pure overhead, and it
   could not write one anyway.

   **Nothing here limits delegation.** A worker cannot delegate because `run_subagent` is
   not bound on this profile, which is the only mechanism that survives a model ignoring
   its instructions. Being absent from the bound list, it is also absent from the tool
   section above, so this prompt does not even mention it.

   Citing matters more here than in the other two profiles: the handles a worker allocates
   are the lead's handles, because it runs on the lead's chat session, and they are how the
   lead's answer points at what the worker actually read.
#}
